year: 2026
abstract: >-
  Video generation models are increasingly viewed as world simulators, which
  requires not only plausible motion but dynamics that respond correctly to
  specified physical parameters. We introduce PhysResponse, a benchmark that
  measures this physical parameter responsiveness at two levels:
  scene-conditioned simulator inversion recovers the effective gravity,
  friction and initial speed of generated motion, and event evaluation tests
  outcomes near and across critical transitions. PhysResponse also provides
  72,000 simulated videos of 20 multi-object interaction types with controlled
  parameters. Evaluated on ten image-to-video models, even the lowest parameter
  errors exceed those of physically correct videos by over an order of
  magnitude, and this failure is invisible to PSNR and SSIM.
keywords:
  - video generation
  - world models
  - physical reasoning
  - benchmark
  - dataset
  - simulator inversion
